<main id="main-content">
<header class="section subpage">
<p class="eyebrow">The person in the workshop</p>
<h1>I’m Danny.<br/>
<em>I care how things work.</em>
</h1>
<p class="article-deck">And how it feels to be on the receiving end of them.</p>
</header>
<section class="section light">
<div class="reading">
<p>I have spent my career inside operations: running teams, fixing broken processes, implementing enterprise systems, and dealing with the gap between what a system was supposed to do and what people actually do to make the business run.</p>
<p>That gap is where I work.</p>
<h2>Exceptional should be repeatable.</h2>
<p>A thoughtful customer experience shouldn’t depend on someone remembering every detail. A good day at work shouldn’t require heroics. And ownership should leave room to think, not just keep everything moving.</p>
<p>I work directly with owners of small founder-led businesses, from understanding the real work through redesign, implementation, and measurement. Sometimes the answer is a clearer decision. Sometimes it is a better workflow. Sometimes it is software, automation, or AI. The experience determines the machinery.</p>
<p>I’m based in Herndon, Virginia.</p>
